1
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
A new angle on the classic tale... And that's no lie!

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
The Adventures of Pinocchio is a family, fantasy,
adventure film directed by Steve Barron.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
One of puppet-maker Geppetto's creations comes magically to life.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
This puppet, Pinocchio, has one major desire and
that is to become a real boy someday.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
In order to accomplish this goal he has to learn to act responsibly.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
This film shows you the adventures on which he learns valuable lessons.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Geppetto, played by Martin Landau.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Pinocchio, played by Jonathan Taylor Thomas.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Leona, played by Geneviève Bujold.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Lorenzini, played by Udo Kier.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
Felinet, played by Bebe Neuwirth.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Volpe, played by Rob Schneider.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
The Adventures of Pinocchio is a 1996 fantasy film directed by Steve Barron and
based on the original 1883 novel of the same name by Carlo Collodi.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Barron collaborated with Sherry Mills, Tom Benedek
and Barry Berman on the screenplay.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
It was a German, French, British and American venture produced by The
Kushner-Locke Company, Pangaea Holdings and Twin Continental Films.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
It stars Martin Landau and Jonathan Taylor Thomas.

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
The film was a critical and commercial failure which led to the sequel, The
New Adventures of Pinocchio, being released straight to video.

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film explores themes of parent child
relationship, italy, love, school, boys.

19
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:21,000
The tone is emotional.
